d25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"26ae2eeefe8ea205d96f7c4693d54bca13f012f8e2116f2863a7996b7a5a0658","event_uuid":"594b19b2-6296-4a7f-bb92-b90abe9d54a7","position":{"commit_sha":"d513513d5c65823e8217a7dd37da78c94c25bc01","position":"1787469844923195001-594b19b2-6296-4a7f-bb92-b90abe9d54a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FIXED — evidence.\n\nDesign chosen: AC1 option (b) recovery extension (load-bearing), option (a) reordering rejected — full rationale in the description. OSS grounding: the idempotent-replay pattern (transactional-outbox consumers, Debezium/Kafka Connect offset-resume, Temporal activity retries, Stripe idempotency keys): best-effort ordering paired with recovery that heals ANY partial-failure ordering, keyed on the deterministic inbound local id.\n\nImplementation: binding_walk.py phase-1b L10 guard swapped one-for-one for _adopt_stands_down(): a marked key is replayed only when marker set == [deterministic adopt id] AND no binding-store entry AND no local ticket (the lost-adopt residue); every other configuration (live local ticket, pending write-ahead entry, foreign/double markers, retired keys) stands down exactly as before. compute_binding_walk_mutations complexity unchanged (ratchet: new=0 increased=0). fsck untouched (AC3): its unbound_jira audit never consulted labels, keeps alerting until the binding exists.\n\nRED evidence (pre-fix, both new replay cells): assert [] == ['REB-3510'] — 'marked-but-unstored key must replay the adopt' (walk-level) and 'runner 2 must replay the lost adopt' (end-to-end two-runner) — exactly the stand-down. The 3 stand-down guard cells passed pre-fix. Post-fix: 24 targeted tests green; full reconciler suite 3186 passed; make lint + make typecheck (mypy 639 files) green. The d103 absence oracle (test_reconcile_once.py) updated: pass 1 now heals the residue, so pass 2's bound off-window probe is answered deterministically with the 404 sentinel — oracles (no create, zero mutations) unchanged.\n\nLanded: Gerrit change 2152 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, submitted), merged as a4886b03fc8cbb5a68cc09328bbb837051850ae7 (commit 'Replay lost adopts instead of standing down', rebar-ticket trailer 2392-9389-39f9-4ca6).\n\ncaused_by attribution: commit 20dd2fb21e ('feat(reconciler): level-triggered ADOPT heals drift class B', rebar-ticket: 5854-b8d4-17be-4bb2) introduced both the adopt path (label stamped in-pass before durable publish, via the reused inbound-create leaf) and the L10 label stand-down whose comment promised 'binding recovery owns re-linking a marked-but-unstored key' — a promise nothing fulfilled until this fix. Closing with --caused-by=5854-b8d4-17be-4bb2.","timestamp":1787467229275760001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787452150481983001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5e0fcfdb-dd17-4f60-8e96-c862bde7c639","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8656-01fe-6f74-44c9"},{"link_uuid":"4b8e5733-c4d1-4027-8e9b-b7aa2f027d1c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1b16-09c0-33ed-44ec"},{"link_uuid":"594b19b2-6296-4a7f-bb92-b90abe9d54a7","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"5854-b8d4-17be-4bb2"}],"description":"Discovered while repairing binding-drift bug 8656-01fe-6f74-44c9 (unbound_jira REB-3510).\n\nDEFECT: the inbound-create adopt path writes the Jira-side rebar-id:<local-id> label BEFORE the local CREATE event + binding are durably published to origin/tickets. When the pass's final tickets push is rejected (non-fast-forward) on an EPHEMERAL runner (GHA run 32602702883: 'final-push-rejected … 7 unpushed commits', runner destroyed), the local state is lost while the Jira label persists. Every automated healing path then stands down:\n- binding_walk L10 guard skips adopt when the rebar-id label is present\n- differ's bug-4354 suppression likewise stands down on the label\n- BindingRecovery.recover_pending_bindings only walks state=='pending' store entries, which were lost with the runner\n\nResult: a permanently stuck unbound_jira drift that only manual repair (or the fsck canary + human) can clear. This class will recur on any ephemeral-runner reconcile that loses its final push race.\n\n## Chosen design (AC1): option (b) — recovery extension, mechanizing the manual repair\n\nCodebase evaluation of the two AC1 options:\n\n- (a) durable-publish-first ordering was evaluated and REJECTED as the load-bearing fix. The label write-back (`_inbound_create_writeback_jira`) runs per-mutation inside `_apply_batch`'s dispatch loop; deferring it until after the pass's final `commit_and_push_tickets_branch` would restructure the apply loop, widen the bug-4354 window (the label is the differ's within-pass and next-pass dedup signal), and STILL leave the mirror-image window (local published, label stamp lost). Notably, that mirror window is ALREADY healed idempotently today: the ticket-1577 dedup guard in `_apply_inbound_create` (binding present -> `dedup_skipped`) makes replay safe when local state survived. The one unhandled ordering is exactly its converse — label persisted, local state lost — so the symmetric completion of the existing idempotent-replay design is the recovery extension, not a reordering.\n- (b) recovery extension is the load-bearing fix. This matches what mature OSS systems do for cross-system crash windows (transactional-outbox consumers, Debezium/Kafka Connect source connectors resuming idempotently from offsets, Temporal activity retries, Stripe idempotent replay): pair best-effort ordering with IDEMPOTENT RECOVERY keyed on a deterministic identity — here the deterministic inbound local id (`_jira_key_to_local_id`), which makes the replayed adopt converge on the same local id, binding, and (idempotent re-add) the same Jira label.\n\nImplementation: the fix lands in `binding_walk.py`'s phase-1b unbound arm — the level-triggered walk that already re-considers every present-unbound key each pass and whose L10 guard comment already promises \"binding recovery owns re-linking a marked-but-unstored key\" (a promise nothing fulfills today). The L10 stand-down becomes conditional: when the unbound key's rebar-id marker set is exactly the DETERMINISTIC inbound id for that key (`jira-<key-lower>`), AND the binding store has no entry (pending or confirmed) for that id, AND a targeted local read (`local_reader`) finds no local ticket — i.e. the marked-but-unstored lost-adopt residue — the walk falls through to the ordinary classify->ADOPT machinery instead of standing down. The replayed adopt routes through the EXISTING `_apply_inbound_create` leaf unchanged (retired-skip gate, dedup guard, baseline seed, idempotent label write-back) and through the existing blast-radius breaker and census.\n\nSafety scoping (why this cannot re-introduce L11 double-bind): a marker that does NOT equal the deterministic inbound id (a UUID from an outbound bind, a foreign `jira-dig-NNNN` ghost label, or multiple markers) keeps the unconditional stand-down — those are different drift classes owned by dd-5 conflict surfacing / fsck alert + human adjudication. A key whose marked id still has a store entry keeps the stand-down (pending-write-ahead recovery owns it). A key whose marked local ticket still exists keeps the stand-down (only the binding is missing — a store_integrity repair, not this class). A RETIRED key still routes to SKIP_RETIRED via the classifier and the leaf's gate #1.\n\n`bridge_fsck` is deliberately untouched (AC3): its unbound_jira audit classifies present-unbound snapshot keys without consulting the label, so it keeps alerting on this class until the binding actually exists again — no suppression.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Recovery extension per option (b): `binding_walk.py`'s unbound arm detects a marked-but-unstored key (rebar-id label equal to the deterministic inbound local id; no binding-store entry for that id; no local ticket) and replays the adopt through the existing inbound-create leaf, instead of standing down on the L10 guard. `compute_binding_walk_mutations` complexity does not increase (guard swapped one-for-one into a helper).\n- [x] A RED-first regression test simulating the lost-final-push runner: runner 1 adopts (CREATE event + binding written, label stamped), the final push is rejected and ALL local state is discarded; runner 2 (fresh store, fresh tracker) sees the labeled snapshot — the walk emits the replay adopt and applying it re-materialises the local ticket + binding under the SAME deterministic local id with no duplicate label. Confirmed failing (walk stands down, adopted == []) before the fix.\n- [x] Existing L10/L11 protections preserved: foreign/ghost markers, multi-marker keys, keys whose marked id still has a store entry, and keys whose marked local ticket still exists all keep standing down; retired keys still skip. Existing tests `test_class_b_labeled_key_not_double_bound` and `test_class_b_empty_rebar_id_marker_is_adopted` unchanged and green.\n- [x] bridge fsck continues to alert unbound_jira on the class until healed — no suppression added anywhere (fsck code untouched; post-heal the key is bound so the alert clears by becoming true).\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_walk.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_inbound_adopt.py -q` — new marked-but-unstored replay cells (walk-level + end-to-end two-runner replay) plus all existing class-A/B/C cells green.\n- RED evidence recorded on the ticket: the new walk-level test fails on pre-fix code with `adopted == []` (stand-down on the label).\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` (includes the complexity ratchet: new=0 increased=0) and `make typecheck` green.\n- fsck behavior verified by reading `bridge_fsck.py`'s unbound_jira audit (label not consulted) — no code change there.\n\nEvidence and full RCA on ticket 8656-01fe-6f74-44c9; repair precedent 16c1-0f0c.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_walk.py","reason":"phase-1b unbound arm: replace the blanket rebar-id-label stand-down with residue detection (marked-but-unstored => replay the adopt)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_walk.py","reason":"walk-level RED regression cell + stand-down guard tests for the marked-but-unstored residue"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_inbound_adopt.py","reason":"end-to-end two-runner lost-final-push replay test"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py","reason":"d103 absence-oracle fixture update: healed pass-2 probe answered deterministically (404 sentinel) instead of relying on the buggy stand-down"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1b16-09c0-33ed-44ec"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"62c511e2-5247-45ab-8693-6a969f987795","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2392-9389-39f9-4ca6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconcile stamps Jira rebar-id label before local adoption is durably published — push-rejected ephemeral runs strand unhealable unbound_jira drift","verify_commands":[]},"so